 Your use of the Teladoc Services and any content accessed through the Teladoc Services must comply with all applicable laws, regulations, and ordinances, including any laws regarding the export of data or software. You must be an adult of the legal age of majority or otherwise authorized under the laws in your jurisdiction or state of residence to enter into binding contracts. If You are under the legal age of majority and not otherwise authorized by the laws in your jurisdiction or state of residence, Your parent or legal guardian must consent. 
 If You use mobile services to enter and maintain Your personal information, You understand that You are responsible for safeguarding and securing Your mobile device and the associated credentials (such as username and password or third-party login credentials). If You leave Your mobile device unattended, or if it is lost or stolen, You understand that Your personal information may be accessible to others. To protect Your confidential health information, it is good practice to enable the best currently-available security features of your mobile device. 
